A   THE ALGEBRA (sympy on generic kernels, then k04's): k04's F3 equation, the fold identity, F6's quantity, the saturated branch
======================================================================================================================
  [PASS] A1 k04's F3 equation re-derived: dL/dr|_Y = r [Zt + (2 - K_B)(s Delta - j)/(8 pi)] (the three-form's conserved conjugate) and J_Y = s/Delta, so the scalar's law J_Y g_phi = g_N is y = s r
         measured: ds/dr|_Y = -Delta/(Deltap*r); conjugate identity True; J_Y = s/Delta True
  [PASS] A2 THE FOLD IDENTITY: on shell L_rr|_Y = Zt N/Delta' and du/ds = N/(1 + cF)^2 with N = Delta'(1 + c(F + s Delta)) - c Delta^2, so the Legendre map q -> Pi at fixed Y degenerates exactly where the slaved force peaks; dy/ds = (1 + c(F - s F'))/(1 + cF)^2, so C_L,eff = dy/du = (1 + c(F - sF'))/N
         measured: du/ds True; L_rr|_Y True; dy/ds True
         reading:  F6's Z_eff = Pi/q = Zt (1 + cF) is the secant; the stability-relevant quantity is the tangent L_rr|_Y ~ N, or C_L,eff ~ 1/N
  [PASS] A3 F6'S QUANTITY IS POSITIVE BY CONSTRUCTION: for k04's kernel F' = Delta - s Delta' = Delta (sqrt(s)/2) e^sqrt(s)/(e^sqrt(s) - 1) > 0 (F' = Delta_sat on the saturated branch) and F(0) = 0, so F >= 0 and F6's Z_eff = Z (1 + cF) >= Z at every s -- whatever the slaved kernel does
         measured: identity (sympy True, 30-digit spot values 0.0e+00) True; F' > 0 on (0, s_sat) True; min F on k04's own 60-point grid 1.054e-05 (k04 printed 1.05e-05); min F on 1e-6..1e4 3.333e-10
         reading:  F = Y J_Y - J >= 0 is the Legendre-positivity of any kernel convex in Y: F6 can only fail for a kernel that is not a kernel
  [PASS] A4 THE SATURATED BRANCH: the flux equation is linear there, r = (1 - c D_sat y)/(1 - c j_sat); the slaved force FALLS at du/dy = -c D_sat^2/(1 - c j_sat) to zero at y_off = 1/(c D_sat); C_L,eff = -(1 - c j_sat)/(c D_sat^2) < 0
         measured: r = (D_sat*c*y - 1)/(c*j_sat - 1); du/dy = D_sat**2*c/(c*j_sat - 1); y_off = 1/(D_sat*c); C_L,eff: K0 -238.62 (y_off 155.23), K25 -272.87 (y_off 177.41), TA -163.05 (y_off 106.29)
         reading:  k04's kernel is FLAT above s_sat (the bounded boost); a0_loc falling with g_N tilts that flat branch downward
  [PASS] A5 THE FLUX EQUATION IS WELL-POSED (the restricted sense of F6): dy/ds = (1 + c(s^2 Delta' - j))/(1 + cF)^2 >= (1 - c j_sat)/(1 + cF)^2 > 0, so r(y) is single-valued: exactly one root, 0 < a0_loc <= a0, at every y below y_off
         measured: F - sF' = s^2 Delta' - j: True; min_s (1 + c(F - sF')): K0 0.99550, K25 0.99606, TA 0.99343

